From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:16:40 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: align scrolling and viewport geometry for native
 clicks

Make CDP scrollIntoViewIfNeeded move the existing window scroller on both
axes, honor an optional element-relative rectangle, and leave visible axes
unchanged. Share ordinary-flow client coordinates with hit testing and
report actual window offsets in CDP viewport metrics. Preserve positioned
coordinates without double subtraction, including synthetic auto-inset
viewport-fixed anchors.

Keep the existing synthetic layout, screenshot dimensions, scroll extents
and input routing. Automatic nested scrolling and general CSS/painting
correctness remain outside scope. Adjust the existing wheel-chain test's
pointer coordinates after viewport scrolling; add no upstream tests.

Validation: ReleaseFast and Debug builds; all 1658 upstream tests; seven
temporary native Playwright probe groups. Native Flux sidebar navigation,
GitHub navigation expansion and Steam agreement checking succeed; Flux
search receives the click. Renovate Clear receives the native click but
still lacks reset activation, outside this viewport fix. Passive benchmark:
123/130, with both explicit rectangle consistency checks passing. One
reviewer finding on auto-inset fixed controls was addressed and validated.
